const e={id:"js-destructuring-spread-rest",title:{en:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:9,sections:[{id:"concept",type:"concept",heading:{en:"Unpacking & Spreading JavaScript Data",hi:"JavaScript Mein Data Unpack Aur Spread Karna"},body:{en:"ES6 introduced three interconnected features that dramatically simplified how developers work with arrays and objects:\n\n1. **Destructuring**: A convenient syntax that extracts multiple values from arrays or properties from objects into distinct variables in a single line.\n2. **Spread Operator (`...`)**: Unpacks an iterable (like an array or object) into individual elements or properties. It is the gold standard for **immutable state updates** in React.\n3. **Rest Operator (`...`)**: Uses the exact same three dots syntax, but does the **opposite of spread**: it condenses multiple elements into a single array. Used in function arguments and destructuring remainders.",hi:"ES6 ne teen aisi features introduce ki jinhone arrays aur objects ke sath kaam karne ko bohot aasan bana diya:\n\n1. **Destructuring**: Ek aisi clean syntax jisse hum ek hi line mein object ki properties ya array ke items nikal kar alag variables mein store kar sakte hain.\n2. **Spread Operator (`...`)**: Yeh kisi array ya object ke andar ke saare elements ko khol kar (unpack karke) naye object ya array mein faila deta hai. React state ko bina mutate kiye update karne ke liye yeh sabse zaroori tool hai.\n3. **Rest Operator (`...`)**: Yeh dikhne mein bilkul spread jaisa teen dots (`...`) hota hai, par iska kaam ulta hota hai: yeh bache hue multiple elements ko ikattha karke ek single array bana deta hai."},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"destructure-overview.js",snippet:`// 1. Object Destructuring with Renaming & Default
const user = { id: 101, username: 'aman_dev', role: 'admin' };
const { username: handle, role, status = 'active' } = user;
console.log(handle); // "aman_dev" (Renamed)
console.log(status); // "active" (Default applied)

// 2. Spread vs Rest
const numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];

// Rest: Gathers remaining elements into an array
const [first, second, ...restOfNumbers] = numbers;
console.log(first); // 10
console.log(restOfNumbers); // [30, 40, 50]

// Spread: Unpacks array into new container
const cloned = [0, ...numbers, 60];
console.log(cloned); // [0, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60]`}},{id:"why-it-matters",type:"concept",heading:{en:"Why Destructuring & Spread are Central to React & MERN",hi:"React Aur MERN Mein Inka Har Jagah Use Kyun Hota Hai?"},body:{en:"Without destructuring and spread:\n- Reading Express request parameters requires typing `req.body.email`, `req.body.password`, `req.body.name` 10 times.\n- Updating React state without mutating memory references requires tedious loops or `Object.assign()`.\n\n**With Destructuring & Spread:**\n- One line cleanly extracts your data: `const { email, password } = req.body;`.\n- One line immutably updates a React state object: `setUser(prev => ({ ...prev, email: newEmail }))`.",hi:"Destructuring aur spread ke bina:\n- Express backend mein baar-baar `req.body.email`, `req.body.password` likhna padta tha.\n- React state ko immutably update karna bohot lamba aur complex tha.\n\n**Inke aane ke baad:**\n- Ek line mein data nikal jata hai: `const { email, password } = req.body;`.\n- Ek line mein React state update hoti hai: `setUser(prev => ({ ...prev, email }))`."}},{id:"analogy",type:"analogy",heading:{en:"The Mumbai Dabbawala Tiffin Analogy",hi:"Mumbai Ke Dabbawala Tiffin Ka Udaharan"},body:{en:`Think of Destructuring and Spread like a multi-tiered steel Indian tiffin box (dabba):

- **The Packed Tiffin (The Object)**: The tiffin arrives containing 3 tiers: Roti, Dal, and Sabzi.
- **Destructuring (Unpacking the Dabba)**: You unlatch the steel clips and place the containers on your table:
  \`const { roti, dal, sabzi } = tiffin;\`. You can now pick up the Roti directly without carrying the whole heavy frame!
- **Spread Operator (Serving onto a Big Thali)**: You take an empty plate, spread the rotis and sabzi onto it, and add a fresh gulab jamun:
  \`const myThali = { ...tiffin, dessert: "Gulab Jamun" };\`. You created a brand new plate without altering the original dabba!`,hi:`Destructuring aur Spread ko **Mumbai Dabbawala ke 3-tier Steel Tiffin** se samjhein:

- **Packed Tiffin (Object)**: Tiffin ke andar teen dabbe band hain—Roti, Daal, aur Sabzi.
- **Destructuring (Tiffin Kholna)**: Aapne clip khola aur teeno dabbe table par alag-alag rakh diye:
  \`const { roti, dal, sabzi } = tiffin;\`. Ab aap seedha roti kha sakte hain bina poora tiffin uthaye.
- **Spread Operator (Thali Mein Parosna)**: Aapne ek nayi thali li, tiffin ka saara khana usme faila diya (spread), aur sath mein ek meetha gulab jamun rakh liya:
  \`const myThali = { ...tiffin, sweet: "Gulab Jamun" };\`. Original tiffin ko bina kharab kiye aapne ek nayi complete thali bana li!`}},{id:"syntax",type:"syntax",heading:{en:"Deep Destructuring & The Shallow Copy Warning",hi:"Deep Destructuring & Shallow Copy Ka Critical Rule"},body:{en:`### Nested Destructuring
You can extract deeply nested properties directly:
\`\`\`javascript
const user = {
  profile: {
    address: { city: 'Bengaluru', pincode: 560001 }
  }
};

const { profile: { address: { city } } } = user;
console.log(city); // "Bengaluru"
\`\`\`

---

### The Shallow Copy Warning!
Spread (\`...\`) creates a **shallow copy**, NOT a deep copy. Primitive values are copied, but nested objects are still copied by **memory reference**:

\`\`\`javascript
const original = { name: 'Aman', location: { city: 'Delhi' } };
const clone = { ...original };

clone.location.city = 'Mumbai'; // MUTATES original.location.city as well!
\`\`\`

To perform a true deep copy in modern JavaScript, use \`structuredClone(original)\`.`,hi:`### Nested Destructuring
Nested objects se direct value nikalne ka tareeqa:
\`\`\`javascript
const user = {
  profile: {
    address: { city: 'Bengaluru', pincode: 560001 }
  }
};

const { profile: { address: { city } } } = user;
console.log(city); // "Bengaluru"
\`\`\`

---

### Shallow Copy Ka Warning!
Spread operator (\`...\`) hamesha **shallow copy** banata hai. Agar object ke andar koi doosra object hai, toh uska reference copy hota hai:

\`\`\`javascript
const original = { name: 'Aman', location: { city: 'Delhi' } };
const clone = { ...original };

clone.location.city = 'Mumbai'; // Isse original object ka city bhi badal jayega!
\`\`\`

Poora deep clone banane ke liye modern JavaScript ka \`structuredClone(original)\` function use karein.`}},{id:"examples",type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 1 (Basic): Destructuring Function Parameters",hi:"Example 1 (Basic): Function Arguments Mein Destructuring"},body:{en:"Instead of accepting a generic `props` object and writing `props.title`, destructure directly inside the parameter list:",hi:"React components mein direct parameters destructure karne ka pattern:"},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"destructure-params.js",snippet:`// Clean function parameter destructuring with default fallback
function renderProductBadge({ title, price, isFeatured = false }) {
  console.log(\`Product: \${title} | Price: ₹\${price} | Featured: \${isFeatured}\`);
}

const product = {
  id: 1,
  title: 'Noise Cancelling Headphones',
  price: 4999,
  brand: 'Sony'
};

renderProductBadge(product);
// Output: Product: Noise Cancelling Headphones | Price: ₹4999 | Featured: false`}},{id:"example-intermediate",type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2 (Intermediate): Immutable Array Operations with Spread",hi:"Example 2 (Intermediate): Array Ko Immutably Manipulate Karna"},body:{en:"Adding, removing, and updating array elements without mutating the original array:",hi:"Original array ko bina chhue naye items add, remove aur update karna:"},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"immutable-array-spread.js",snippet:`const initialTags = ['react', 'node', 'express'];

// 1. Insert at end (push equivalent)
const withMongo = [...initialTags, 'mongodb'];

// 2. Insert at beginning (unshift equivalent)
const withJs = ['javascript', ...initialTags];

// 3. Insert in middle at index 2
const insertedMiddle = [
  ...initialTags.slice(0, 2),
  'typescript',
  ...initialTags.slice(2)
];

console.log(insertedMiddle);
// Output: ['react', 'node', 'typescript', 'express']
console.log(initialTags); // Still ['react', 'node', 'express'] (Original untouched!)`}},{id:"example-real-world",type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3 (Real-World): Clean Express Route Handler",hi:"Example 3 (Real-World): Production Express Route Destructuring"},body:{en:"Combining destructuring with rest parameters to sanitize sensitive user input before saving to the database:",hi:"Express route mein destructuring aur rest use karke sensitive data filter karna:"},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"express-destructure-sanitize.js",snippet:`// Express controller: Update User Profile
async function updateUserProfile(req, res) {
  // Destructure route param and body fields
  const { id } = req.params;
  
  // Extract sensitive fields to prevent privilege escalation attacks!
  // Even if a hacker sends 'role: admin' or 'passwordHash', we separate them!
  const { role, passwordHash, ...safeUpdateFields } = req.body;

  try {
    const updatedUser = await User.findByIdAndUpdate(
      id,
      { $set: safeUpdateFields },
      { new: true, runValidators: true }
    );

    if (!updatedUser) {
      return res.status(404).json({ error: "User not found" });
    }

    return res.status(200).json({ success: true, data: updatedUser });
  } catch (error) {
    return res.status(500).json({ error: error.message });
  }
}`}},{id:"mistakes",type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"Common Destructuring Pitfalls",hi:"Destructuring Ki Common Galtiyan"},body:{en:"### 1. Destructuring from undefined or null\n- **The Crash**: `const { name } = undefined;` throws `TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'name' of undefined`.\n- **The Fix**: Always provide a default empty object fallback:\n```javascript\nconst { name } = maybeUndefinedUser || {};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Confusing Rest with Spread\n- **Spread (`...`)**: Unpacks. Used in calls: `Math.max(...nums)` or array literals: `[...arr]`.\n- **Rest (`...`)**: Packs. Used in function parameters: `function(...args)` or destructuring remainders: `const [first, ...rest] = arr;`.",hi:"### 1. undefined Se Destructure Karna\n- **Crash**: `const { name } = undefined;` se app crash ho jati hai (`TypeError`).\n- **Solution**: Hamesha fallback empty object provide karein:\n```javascript\nconst { name } = user || {};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Spread Aur Rest Mein Confusion\n- **Spread**: Cheezon ko khol kar failata hai (`[...arr]`).\n- **Rest**: Bache hue elements ko pack karke ek array banata hai (`(...args)`)."}},{id:"best-practices",type:"summary",heading:{en:"Best Practices",hi:"Best Practices"},body:{en:"- Destructure `props` directly in React component signatures.\n- Use default values to prevent undefined errors.\n- Remember spread is shallow; use `structuredClone()` for deeply nested objects.\n- Use rest operator to remove sensitive fields when updating database records.",hi:`- React components ke parameter mein direct props destructure karein.
- Undefined se bachne ke liye default values zaroor use karein.
- Yaad rakhein spread shallow copy banata hai.
- Sensitive fields hatane ke liye rest operator ka use karein.`}},{id:"interview",type:"interview",heading:{en:"Destructuring & Spread Interview Questions",hi:"Destructuring & Spread Interview Questions"},body:{en:"Frequently asked questions in full-stack coding rounds:",hi:"Full-stack interviews mein puche jane wale top questions:"},questions:[{q:{en:"What is the difference between a Shallow Copy and a Deep Copy?",hi:"Shallow Copy aur Deep Copy mein kya technical farq hota hai?"},a:{en:"A Shallow Copy (created via {...obj} or Object.assign()) only duplicates the top-level primitive properties into a new memory container. Any nested objects or arrays inside it are copied by REFERENCE. If you mutate a nested object in the clone, the original object's nested data is also mutated. A Deep Copy (via structuredClone()) recursively duplicates all nested objects, guaranteeing complete independence in memory.",hi:"Shallow Copy (jaise {...obj}) sirf pehli layer ke primitives ko copy karta hai. Agar andar koi doosra object hai, toh uska pointer copy hota hai. Isliye andar ka data badalne par dono objects badal jaate hain. Deep Copy (`structuredClone()`) poore tree ko recursively naye memory address par copy karta hai."},takeaway:{en:"Shallow copies share nested object references; deep copies clone the entire tree.",hi:"Shallow copy nested references share karta hai; deep copy sab kuch independently clone karta hai."}}]},{id:"summary",type:"summary",heading:{en:"Quick Summary",hi:"Quick Summary"},body:{en:"- Destructuring unpacks arrays and objects into named variables.\n- Spread (`...`) creates new array/object copies without mutation.\n- Rest (`...`) captures remaining items into a single array.\n- Always provide fallback defaults when destructuring nullable objects.",hi:"- Destructuring data ko unpack karke variables banata hai.\n- Spread (`...`) bina mutate kiye naye copies banata hai.\n- Rest (`...`) bache hue elements ko bundle karta hai.\n- Undefined errors se bachne ke liye default fallbacks lagayein."}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"Given: const { city = 'Delhi' } = { city: undefined }; what is the value of city?",hi:"const { city = 'Delhi' } = { city: undefined }; mein city ki value kya hogi?"},options:[{en:"'Delhi'",hi:"'Delhi'"},{en:"undefined",hi:"undefined"},{en:"null",hi:"null"},{en:"Throws TypeError",hi:"TypeError aayega"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"In JavaScript default parameter and destructuring evaluation, the default value triggers ONLY if the property is undefined (or missing). Since city was undefined, the default 'Delhi' applies.",hi:"JavaScript mein default value tabhi trigger hoti hai jab property `undefined` ya missing ho. Isliye default value 'Delhi' lag jayegi."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling destructuring, rest & spread operators with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators directly resolve?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Modular design Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators in production?",hi:"Production mein Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}},{question:{en:"Why is thorough resource cleanup (clearing timers, closing sockets, aborting in-flight requests) critical in Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators mein resource cleanup (timers clear karna, sockets band karna, network abort karna) kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"To prevent memory leaks where unreachable or orphaned objects remain retained in heap memory, causing gradual performance degradation and crashes",hi:"Memory leaks rokne ke liye taaki unneeded objects RAM mein jama na hon aur server crash na ho"},{en:"To delete the client's local disk partition",hi:"Client ka local disk partition delete karne ke liye"},{en:"Because JavaScript engines allow only 5 variables in RAM",hi:"JS engine sirf 5 variables allow karta hai"},{en:"Cleanup is unnecessary because garbage collection handles 100% of event listeners automatically",hi:"Cleanup ki zaroorat nahi hoti"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Unclosed connections and dangling event listeners create references that prevent garbage collection, leading to severe memory leaks over time.",hi:"Dangling listeners aur unclosed connections memory leaks banate hain jo V8 heap ko exhaust karke process crash kar dete hain."}},{question:{en:"What principle enables Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators to operate identically across local dev, staging, and production environments?",hi:"Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators ko local dev, staging aur production mein bilkul same operate karne ke liye kaunsa niyam zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Twelve-Factor App methodology: injecting all environment-specific configurations and credentials via environment variables rather than hardcoded code",hi:"Twelve-Factor niyam: environment variables se dynamic configuration aur credentials inject karna bina code badle"},{en:"Manually rewriting the codebase before deploying to each server",hi:"Har server par deploy karne se pehle naya code likhna"},{en:"Hosting development and production on the same physical developer laptop",hi:"Ek hi laptop par dev aur prod dono host karna"},{en:"Disabling all security authentications in production environments",hi:"Production mein saari security band kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Decoupling configuration from executable code allows identical, immutable container images to run reliably across all deployment stages.",hi:"Config aur code ko alag rakhne se ek hi build image bina kisi bug ke kisi bhi cloud platform par chal sakti hai."}},{question:{en:"When an unexpected outage or regression occurs in production involving Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators, what is the first engineering step?",hi:"Production mein Destructuring, Rest & Spread Operators se related outage ya regression aane par pehla engineering step kya hona chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Immediately delete all production databases without backups",hi:"Bina backup ke production database delete kar dena"},{en:"Check centralized observability logs and error stack traces, correlate request IDs, reproduce locally with minimal test cases, and isolate the root cause",hi:"Centralized observability logs aur stack traces check karna, request ID correlate karna, aur locally minimal test cases se reproduce karna"},{en:"Blame the operating system without inspecting any server logs",hi:"Bina log dekhe OS ko blame karna"},{en:"Wait several days hoping the system resolves itself",hi:"Kai din intezar karna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Disciplined engineering incident response begins with analyzing structured logs, tracing request flow, and isolating reproducible root causes.",hi:"Disciplined debugging structured logs aur request correlation ID dekh kar root cause isolate karne se shuru hoti hai."}}]};export{e as default};
